lines 35485+35569 had an unquoted ': ' inside the exp3833 verdict
(result: complete: ldt_gap_...), making YAML parse it as a nested mapping. That broke
test_docs.py (which parses the YAML), and the conductor's smart-subset pre-test gate runs
test_docs.py on every task -> '1 failed, N passed' SKIP-cascaded every experiment from
.350 onward. FIX: quote both values. Pretest subset now 81 passed / 0 failed; the full
YAML parses. Second cause (gemini-CLI crash on the archive task) routed around in .356 by
all-codex+requires_codex.

Staged milestone .356 (research-roadmap-next.yaml, 12 tasks exp3857-exp3868): re-issues the
verifier-MOAT durability adjudication (Deep-Think P2) the wipeout prevented -- build the
balanced step-error corpus, run the error-independence scissor AT SCALE with bootstrap CI +
positive controls, MEASURE verifier-vs-reasoner independence (arXiv:2604.07650); plus a
NEW-architecture graph-grounding facts prototype, FR-11 v23 online independence-reweighting
(self-learning MANDATE), LDT-margin sharpening, and the two non-terminal FPGA boards.
paper_ready stays TRUE; frozen FoVer 0.9131 unchanged. Design: research-roadmap-v356.md.

